## Building a Figma file from the “existing users AI migration” flow

**Inputs already in-repo:**

- **FigJam flow** — Created via MCP `generate_diagram` (“Existing users AI migration flows”). Open the **claim link** from the tool response in FigJam, then **duplicate** or **link** it from your deliverable file.  
- **Screen inventory** — [`Knowledge/Tasks/DESIGN-BRIEF-AI-Migration-Figma-mondayDS.md`](../../Knowledge/Tasks/DESIGN-BRIEF-AI-Migration-Figma-mondayDS.md) (flows **A–H**).  
- **Pricing visual reference** — [Pricing page with AI](https://www.figma.com/design/DIyM0lkmlwnzMkTI0AZKs8/Pricing-page-with-AI?node-id=26815-11134&m=dev) (`fileKey` `DIyM0lkmlwnzMkTI0AZKs8`).

**Recommended Figma file structure (designer execution):**

1. **Cover** — Initiative title + links to PRD + FigJam.  
2. **Flow** — Paste **FigJam** diagram or embed link.  
3. **Pages** — One page per flow **A–H** (May 6 discovery, CTA, 80% top-up, add-on migration modal, high usage, overlap, agents, post-promo).  
4. **Components** — Instance **monday DS**; reuse **one** migration **price module** for add-on + high-usage variants (copy only).  
5. **Ready for dev** — Mark frames; note flag keys in description.

**Figma Make:** For **prompt-generated** UI explorations, use **Figma Make** in the browser per org workflow; this repo does **not** store Make sources. Export screenshots into `Knowledge/Tasks/` if needed for reviews.

